f(x)=\frac{1\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+5\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{2-\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\csc\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}=\frac{1\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+5\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{2-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}
Using the quotient rule to differentiate we get,
f'(x)=\frac{d}{dx}(\frac{1\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+5\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{2-\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\csc\mathopen{}\left(x\right)})=1\frac{\frac{d}{dx}[\left(x^{2}+5\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)]\cdot (2-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right))-\frac{d}{dx}[2-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)]\cdot \left(x^{2}+5\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{(2-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right))^2}
=1\frac{[2x\cdot \cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right) - \csc^{2}\mathopen{}\left(x\right) \cdot (x^{2}+5)]\cdot  (2-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right))-[\csc^{2}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)]\cdot \left(x^{2}+5\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{(2-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right))^2}
=\frac{4x\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)-2\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+5\right)\csc^{2}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)-2x\cot^{2}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{\left(2-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\right)^{2}}
